  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-image-resizer",
      "text": "A small client-only plugin for DeepSeek Harness Web. It proportionally downsizes oversized conversation images before DSH's native attachment admission, so ordinary Retina/full-screen screenshots can be pasted or dropped without changing DSH core limits."
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "- PNG, JPEG, and WebP images with a side above `2000px` are resized in the browser.\n- Aspect ratio, file name, media type, and `lastModified` metadata are preserved.\n- Images already within the limit are passed through without re-encoding.\n- GIF and unsupported image types are not transformed, avoiding animation loss or silent format conversion.\n- If browser decoding/encoding fails, the original image is replayed into DSH so the native validation/error path remains authoritative.\n- Paste text accompanying an image is inserted immediately at the original caret; normalized files follow asynchronously.\n- All listeners are owned by the Cordis client fiber and are removed when the plugin stops."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/HaijieChen/dsh-image-resizer.git\ncd dsh-image-resizer\npnpm install\npnpm test\npnpm build\ndsh plugin --profile web add link:$(pwd)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Restart the existing dsh web process normally, then refresh its page.",
      "text": "```\n\nThe plugin does not modify DSH source, attachment storage, model routes, or the Host's `maxImageDimension` policy."
    }
  ],
